# Files kept out of the published package.
#
# Everything here is needed to *rebuild* Skribble, not to *use* it. The
# regeneration sources are the bulk of the archive: `tool/font` alone is several
# megabytes of upstream Recursive desktop fonts and intermediate static
# instances that only `roughen_fonts.dart` reads. Consumers get the finished
# faces from `assets/fonts`.
#
# `pub publish` unions this file with .gitignore, so entries never ship even if
# they are tracked in Git.
tool/
example/
build/
